\begin_layout Plain Layout

\series bold
Exercise 5.16
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Repeat Exercise 5.15,
 but this time,
 calculate entropy in bits.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
#+html:
 <details><summary>Show/hide solution...</summary>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The Shannon entropy for this example is
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
S_{s} & =-p(0)\log_{2}\left(p(0)\right)-p(1)\cdot\log_{2}\left(p(1)\right)=-\frac{1}{2}\log_{2}\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)-\frac{1}{2}\cdot\log_{2}\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)\\
 & =-\log_{2}\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)=-\left(-1\right)=1
\end{align*}

\end_inset

For the fair coin toss,
 we have one bit of entropy.
 That is,
 we lack one bit of information about the outcome of the measurement.
\end_layout

